\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Class breakdown of the 8,474,531-galaxy catalog. The three-class output is dominated by the \textsc  {not\_spiral}{}/edge-on class (60.8\% raw, 62.2\% post-equivariance), which captures ellipticals, irregulars, edge-on disks, and artifacts. Among the equivariant-classified spirals ($N_{\rm  spiral}^{\rm  eq} = 3{,}201{,}160$ = 1{,}592{,}107~\textsc  {cw}{} + 1{,}609{,}053~\textsc  {ccw}), the CW and CCW fractions are 50.8\% and 49.2\% (raw, Catalog~A) or 49.74\% and 50.26\% (equivariant, Catalog~C), consistent with exact parity. }}{12}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:class_pie}{{5}{12}{Class breakdown of the 8,474,531-galaxy catalog. The three-class output is dominated by the \NS {}/edge-on class (60.8\% raw, 62.2\% post-equivariance), which captures ellipticals, irregulars, edge-on disks, and artifacts. Among the equivariant-classified spirals ($N_{\rm spiral}^{\rm eq} = 3{,}201{,}160$ = 1{,}592{,}107~\CW {} + 1{,}609{,}053~\CCW ), the CW and CCW fractions are 50.8\% and 49.2\% (raw, Catalog~A) or 49.74\% and 50.26\% (equivariant, Catalog~C), consistent with exact parity}{figure.5}{}}
