\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {IV}{\ignorespaces Angular power spectrum of the chirality asymmetry map (Catalog~C, equivariant). The first row is the canonical \emph  {single-mode} $\ell \!=\!1$ post-MASTER result that anchors the dipole-parity null (companion artifact \artifact  {pipelines/p2\_chirality/master\_results/master\_power\_spectrum.json}, $\ell _1$\,dipole entry; analysis subsample $n\!=\!5{,}547{,}858$, $f_{\rm  sky}\!=\!0.659$). Rows 2--5 are five-mode \emph  {bandpowers} $\ell \!\in \![\ell _{\rm  eff}\!-\!2,\,\ell _{\rm  eff}\!+\!2]$ from the canonical-$N$ MASTER recompute on the full $N_{\rm  spiral}\!=\!3{,}201{,}160$ / $f_{\rm  sky}\!=\!0.491$ analysis (companion artifact \artifact  {pipelines/p2\_chirality/r42\_results/wave\_14\_pp\_namaster\_verification.json}; $500$ MC realizations). $\sigma _{\rm  null}$ is the per-bin standard deviation of the MC null distribution at that bandpower. Higher-bandpower $\sim \!2\sigma $ values reflect residual coupling of the $9.5\sigma $ monopole into low-$\ell $ bandpowers under the partial-sky MASTER kernel; the dipole-parity observable is the single-mode $\ell \!=\!1$ result (first row), and the bandpower table is a null-consistency cross-check at multipoles \emph  {other than} the dipole. The canonical-$N$ MASTER direct-MC at $\ell \!=\!1$ on the equivariant map (v1.0.62 closure of the prior post-arXiv TODO) yields $\sigma _{\rm  canonical}\!=\!+1.85$ at $f_{\rm  sky}\!=\!0.4938$, $N_{\rm  spiral}\!=\!3{,}201{,}160$, SEED$\,=\,42$, $500$-MC (Sec.~\ref {sec:conclusions} and companion artifact \artifact  {pipelines/p2\_chirality/outputs/canonical\_provenance/canonical\_n\_master\_l1\_direct.json}); this is a mild canonical-mask excess interpreted as a leakage-floor calibration, with the $-0.122\sigma $ subsample-mask figure retained as the headline post-MASTER null because its $f_{\rm  sky}\!=\!0.659$ mask is a strict superset that bypasses the canonical-mask leakage channel.}}{15}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:multipole}{{IV}{15}{Angular power spectrum of the chirality asymmetry map (Catalog~C, equivariant). The first row is the canonical \emph {single-mode} $\ell \!=\!1$ post-MASTER result that anchors the dipole-parity null (companion artifact \artifact {pipelines/p2\_chirality/master\_results/master\_power\_spectrum.json}, $\ell _1$\,dipole entry; analysis subsample $n\!=\!5{,}547{,}858$, $f_{\rm sky}\!=\!0.659$). Rows 2--5 are five-mode \emph {bandpowers} $\ell \!\in \![\ell _{\rm eff}\!-\!2,\,\ell _{\rm eff}\!+\!2]$ from the canonical-$N$ MASTER recompute on the full $N_{\rm spiral}\!=\!3{,}201{,}160$ / $f_{\rm sky}\!=\!0.491$ analysis (companion artifact \artifact {pipelines/p2\_chirality/r42\_results/wave\_14\_pp\_namaster\_verification.json}; $500$ MC realizations). $\sigma _{\rm null}$ is the per-bin standard deviation of the MC null distribution at that bandpower. Higher-bandpower $\sim \!2\sigmaunit $ values reflect residual coupling of the $9.5\sigmaunit $ monopole into low-$\ell $ bandpowers under the partial-sky MASTER kernel; the dipole-parity observable is the single-mode $\ell \!=\!1$ result (first row), and the bandpower table is a null-consistency cross-check at multipoles \emph {other than} the dipole. The canonical-$N$ MASTER direct-MC at $\ell \!=\!1$ on the equivariant map (v1.0.62 closure of the prior post-arXiv TODO) yields $\sigma _{\rm canonical}\!=\!+1.85$ at $f_{\rm sky}\!=\!0.4938$, $N_{\rm spiral}\!=\!3{,}201{,}160$, SEED$\,=\,42$, $500$-MC (Sec.~\ref {sec:conclusions} and companion artifact \artifact {pipelines/p2\_chirality/outputs/canonical\_provenance/canonical\_n\_master\_l1\_direct.json}); this is a mild canonical-mask excess interpreted as a leakage-floor calibration, with the $-0.122\sigmaunit $ subsample-mask figure retained as the headline post-MASTER null because its $f_{\rm sky}\!=\!0.659$ mask is a strict superset that bypasses the canonical-mask leakage channel}{table.4}{}}
\citation{Gross:2010}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Angular power spectrum of the chirality asymmetry map (Catalog~C, equivariant) for multipoles $\ell = 1$--$5$. Black points show the measured $C_\ell $ values; the gray band indicates the $1\sigma $ and $2\sigma $ envelopes from 1{,}000 Monte Carlo null realizations. Note: the figure as plotted shows the original raw pseudo-$C_\ell $ ($\ell =1$ at $2.75\sigma $ relative to the original shot-noise floor). After the corrected $N_{\rm  spiral}$ normalization the pseudo-$C_\ell $ SNR is $6.48\sigma $ and the MASTER-decoupled value is $6.08\sigma $; however, these are intermediate estimators before full mode-coupling inversion. The headline result (Sec.~\ref {sec:dipole}) is the post-MASTER deconvolution significance of $-0.12\sigma $ on the analysis subsample mask. The v1.0.62 canonical-$N$ direct-MC result $+1.85\sigma $ (Sec.~\ref {sec:conclusions}, $f_{\rm  sky}=0.4938$, $N_{\rm  spiral}=3{,}201{,}160$, $500$-MC, SEED $=42$; supersedes the v1.0.55 analytic projection $+0.26\sigma $) is a mild canonical-mask excess interpreted as a leakage-floor calibration, not as a primordial signal; the no-dipole-at-$\ell =1$ verdict is carried by the full-sky $0.43\sigma $ and strict-superset $-0.12\sigma $ figures which bypass the canonical-mask leakage channel. The $6.48\sigma $/$6.08\sigma $ values reflect mask-induced mode coupling explicitly removed by MASTER deconvolution and should not be quoted as a detection. Verification artifact: \artifact  {pipelines/h200\_results/wave11c\_nspiral\_recompute\_2026-05-01/results.json}. All higher multipoles are consistent with noise. The absence of coherent power at any scale beyond the lowest bin rules out a large-scale parity-violation \emph  {dipole} above the ${\sim }0.29\%$ statistical Fisher / level (minimum detectable at $3\sigma $); the spatially uniform monopole offset (across all 7 equatorial coordinate slabs) is $0.26\%$ (see Sec.~\ref {sec:cw_frac}). }}{17}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:multipoles}{{8}{17}{Angular power spectrum of the chirality asymmetry map (Catalog~C, equivariant) for multipoles $\ell = 1$--$5$. Black points show the measured $C_\ell $ values; the gray band indicates the $1\sigmaunit $ and $2\sigmaunit $ envelopes from 1{,}000 Monte Carlo null realizations. Note: the figure as plotted shows the original raw pseudo-$C_\ell $ ($\ell =1$ at $2.75\sigmaunit $ relative to the original shot-noise floor). After the corrected $N_{\rm spiral}$ normalization the pseudo-$C_\ell $ SNR is $6.48\sigma $ and the MASTER-decoupled value is $6.08\sigma $; however, these are intermediate estimators before full mode-coupling inversion. The headline result (Sec.~\ref {sec:dipole}) is the post-MASTER deconvolution significance of $-0.12\sigmaunit $ on the analysis subsample mask. The v1.0.62 canonical-$N$ direct-MC result $+1.85\sigmaunit $ (Sec.~\ref {sec:conclusions}, $f_{\rm sky}=0.4938$, $N_{\rm spiral}=3{,}201{,}160$, $500$-MC, SEED $=42$; supersedes the v1.0.55 analytic projection $+0.26\sigmaunit $) is a mild canonical-mask excess interpreted as a leakage-floor calibration, not as a primordial signal; the no-dipole-at-$\ell =1$ verdict is carried by the full-sky $0.43\sigmaunit $ and strict-superset $-0.12\sigmaunit $ figures which bypass the canonical-mask leakage channel. The $6.48\sigma $/$6.08\sigma $ values reflect mask-induced mode coupling explicitly removed by MASTER deconvolution and should not be quoted as a detection. Verification artifact: \artifact {pipelines/h200\_results/wave11c\_nspiral\_recompute\_2026-05-01/results.json}. All higher multipoles are consistent with noise. The absence of coherent power at any scale beyond the lowest bin rules out a large-scale parity-violation \emph {dipole} above the ${\sim }0.29\%$ statistical Fisher / level (minimum detectable at $3\sigmaunit $); the spatially uniform monopole offset (across all 7 equatorial coordinate slabs) is $0.26\%$ (see Sec.~\ref {sec:cw_frac})}{figure.8}{}}
